// WRC (Write-to-Read Causality), all-relaxed.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity / Multicopy atomic).
// Source: Sarkar et al., "Understanding POWER Multiprocessors" (PLDI 2011);
//         Alglave et al., "Herding Cats" (TOPLAS 2014).
//
// P0 writes x. P1 reads it and writes y. P2 reads y and then reads x stale.
// The baseline WRC shape, with no ordering inside P1 or P2; the dependency
// variant WRC+data+addr.lit is the one that isolates multicopy atomicity.
//
// Reference verdicts: SC, x86-TSO, ARMv8 (MCA) FORBID.
//                     POWER, ARMv7, C11, RC11 ALLOW.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x := 1
} ||| {
  r1 := x;
  y := 1
} ||| {
  r2 := y;
  r3 := x
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 1 && r3 = 0) [Power]
